{
  "source_file": "HS PROJECT OVERVIEW.pdf",
  "source_section": "0904–0910 — Spices",
  "source_note": "Extracted from the uploaded PDF (Chapter 09 complete code structure, pages 8–12). Descriptions are preserved from the source text; no additional classification rules were inferred.",
  "chapter_notes": [
    {
      "note_id": "CH09-NOTE-1a",
      "text": "Mixtures of two or more products of the same heading remain in that heading.",
      "source_reference": "PDF page 4–5, Chapter 09 notes"
    },
    {
      "note_id": "CH09-NOTE-1b",
      "text": "Mixtures of two or more products of different headings within 0904 to 0910 go to heading 0910.",
      "source_reference": "PDF page 4–5, Chapter 09 notes"
    },
    {
      "note_id": "CH09-NOTE-2",
      "text": "The addition of other substances does not automatically remove classification from Chapter 09 if the resulting goods retain the essential character of the spices.",
      "source_reference": "PDF page 4–5, Chapter 09 notes"
    },
    {
      "note_id": "CH09-NOTE-3",
      "text": "If the resulting product no longer retains the essential character of goods of Chapter 09, it is not classified in Chapter 09; mixed condiments or mixed seasonings go to heading 2103.",
      "source_reference": "PDF page 4–5, Chapter 09 notes"
    },
    {
      "note_id": "CH09-NOTE-4",
      "text": "Chapter 09 does not cover cubeb pepper (Piper cubeba) or other products of heading 1211.",
      "source_reference": "PDF page 5, Chapter 09 notes"
    },
    {
      "note_id": "CH09-SUPP-1",
      "text": "\"Spice\" includes vegetable products rich in essential oils and aromatic principles used mainly as condiments, and they may be whole, crushed, or powdered.",
      "source_reference": "PDF page 5, supplementary notes"
    },
    {
      "note_id": "CH09-SUPP-2",
      "text": "The addition of other substances to spices does not remove them from spice classification if the resulting mixtures retain the essential character of spices; products commonly known as \"masalas\" may still remain in spices depending on that essential-character test.",
      "source_reference": "PDF page 5, supplementary notes"
    }
  ],
